{"quote_id":"KECA-CUR-021","corpus_id":"S002","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"The KECA Radio Talks","source_year":1951,"source_slug":"keca_radio_talks","source_section":"Broadcast 4 — Meditation","quote_original":"All that meditation amounts to is a controlled imagination and a well sustained attention.","primary_topic":"MEDITATION","secondary_topics":["IMAGINATION","ATTENTION"],"tags":["meditation","imagination","attention"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_keca_radio_talks.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"KECA-CUR-029","corpus_id":"S002","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"The KECA Radio Talks","source_year":1951,"source_slug":"keca_radio_talks","source_section":"Broadcast 4 — Meditation","quote_original":"The undisciplined man’s attention is the servant of his vision rather than its master. It is captured by the pressing rather than the important.","primary_topic":"ATTENTION","secondary_topics":["DISCIPLINE"],"tags":["attention","discipline","focus"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_keca_radio_talks.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"KECA-CUR-030","corpus_id":"S002","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"The KECA Radio Talks","source_year":1951,"source_slug":"keca_radio_talks","source_section":"Broadcast 5 — The Law of Assumption","quote_original":"Therefore, the assumption of the wish fulfilled should make you see the world mentally as you would physically were your assumption a physical fact.","primary_topic":"ASSUMPTION","secondary_topics":["WISH_FULFILLED"],"tags":["assumption","wish-fulfilled","mental-view"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_keca_radio_talks.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"KECA-CUR-023","corpus_id":"S002","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"The KECA Radio Talks","source_year":1951,"source_slug":"keca_radio_talks","source_section":"Broadcast 6 — Truth","quote_original":"Our concept of ourselves determines the scenery of our lives.","primary_topic":"SELF_CONCEPT","secondary_topics":["ATTITUDE"],"tags":["self-concept","life","scenery"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_keca_radio_talks.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"KECA-CUR-031","corpus_id":"S002","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"The KECA Radio Talks","source_year":1951,"source_slug":"keca_radio_talks","source_section":"Broadcast 8 — Feeling Is The Secret (Radio Broadcast)","quote_original":"Feeling is the secret of successful prayer, for in prayer, we feel ourselves into the situation of the answered prayer and, then, we live and act upon that conviction.","primary_topic":"FEELING","secondary_topics":["PRAYER"],"tags":["feeling","answered-prayer","conviction"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_keca_radio_talks.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"KECA-CUR-032","corpus_id":"S002","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"The KECA Radio Talks","source_year":1951,"source_slug":"keca_radio_talks","source_section":"Broadcast 8 — Feeling Is The Secret (Radio Broadcast)","quote_original":"The world that moves us is the one we imagine, not the world that surrounds us.","primary_topic":"IMAGINATION","secondary_topics":["FEELING"],"tags":["imagination","world","perception"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_keca_radio_talks.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"KECA-CUR-033","corpus_id":"S002","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"The KECA Radio Talks","source_year":1951,"source_slug":"keca_radio_talks","source_section":"Broadcast 9 — Affirm the Reality of Our Own Greatness","quote_original":"Man is constantly looking about his world and asking, ‘What’s to be done? What will happen?’ when he should ask himself ‘Who am I? What is my concept of myself?’","primary_topic":"SELF_CONCEPT","secondary_topics":["ATTITUDE"],"tags":["self-concept","identity","question"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_keca_radio_talks.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"KECA-CUR-034","corpus_id":"S002","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"The KECA Radio Talks","source_year":1951,"source_slug":"keca_radio_talks","source_section":"Broadcast 9 — Affirm the Reality of Our Own Greatness","quote_original":"Our thoughts are the natural outpouring of our ideas, and our innermost ideas are the man himself.","primary_topic":"THOUGHT","secondary_topics":["SELF_CONCEPT"],"tags":["thought","ideas","self-concept"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_keca_radio_talks.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
